# MyoTTV11: round-10 options for the table-tennis skill (MyoTTV10Skill), each
# opt-in by params; with every switch at 0 it is MyoTTV10Skill (and so the
# round-5 champions, serve for serve).
#
# Round 10 measured where P2 is lost (out/tt_r10/champ_710000.jsonl, 600
# serves of the round-5 champion, 30.3 %). The success rate falls with the
# serve's speed: 50 / 44 / 24 / 13 / 7 % over the speed quintiles, the hit
# rate flat (72-89 %). A fast serve is hit and comes back too fast: the
# return's speed follows the ball's (a still pad returns ~0.95 of it), and
# above ~5.5 m/s the set of pad pitches whose return still clears the net
# and lands narrows to 8-13 degrees (25 degrees at 5 m/s), against a face
# that arrives 10 degrees (1 sigma) off its aim. The pad's velocity along
# its normal at contact (mean -0.4 forehand, +0.2 backhand, sigma 0.5 m/s)
# is uncontrolled and the aim law assumes a still pad.
#
#   pv       the pelvis as a speed governor (1 on): the fore-aft slide reaches
#            its height-matching goal AT contact still moving away from the
#            net (retreating with the ball) at u = pv_k (|v| - pv_v0) + pv_u0
#            m/s, clamped to [pv_lo, pv_max], |v| the ball's predicted speed
#            at the pad's plane. The pad then meets the ball moving with it,
#            which lowers the return's speed by ~u and widens the pitch
#            window (offline best retreat: 0.47 (v - 4.83) m/s on both
#            sides). The aim law expects pv_g u of pad velocity along +x.
#            pv_margin: the slide's goal time is the ball's arrival less this;
#            pv_tmin: inside this time to go the slide coasts.
#            pv 2: the slide's goal is stable. The champion's height matching
#            chases the pad's measured plane (the arm reaches 8-13 cm toward
#            the net in the last 0.1 s and the pelvis retreats to cancel it:
#            the late reversal that leaves it at +-1 m/s at contact); here the
#            goal is the plane where the rising ball passes the pad's height
#            (from the height matching's own choice) less the pad's offset from
#            the pelvis at the start plus pv_reach (the arm's reach by contact),
#            and the retreat is u less the arm's own mean (pv_arm1 forehand,
#            pv_arm2 backhand: what the arm and trunk add to the pad's velocity
#            along +x at contact).
#            pv 3: the slide is predictive. The arm's velocity relative to the
#            pelvis (the paddle's world velocity less the pelvis's, smoothed by
#            pv_sm per tick) is measured and carried to contact: the pelvis's
#            goal is where the pad plane must be less the pad's offset from the
#            pelvis now and the arm's reach over the time to go (looking ahead at
#            most pv_h s, weighted in from pv_h2 s to pv_h2 - pv_hw s before
#            contact), and its terminal velocity is what makes the PAD's velocity
#            along its normal u: (u - arm . n - vy_pelvis n_y) / n_x. The aim law
#            expects the pad's predicted world velocity (pv_g of it).

#   sg       the servo's targets from the goal plane (1 on): the servo's pad
#            height and the aim law's flight come from the ball's state where the
#            height matching will put the pad's plane (the parent's plan is at
#            the plane the pad has NOW; the pelvis is still sliding fore-aft
#            when the servo starts, so the height target slides 5-15 cm over
#            the next 0.15 s and the integral servo chases it, overshooting: the
#            pad drops to 1.09 m at 0.4 s and is back at 1.19 m at contact, its
#            height at contact sd 6-7 cm). Needs g_hx 1.

#   qa       yaw-only servo (1 on): the aim law's normal keeps the pad's own
#            pitch (the z component of its measured normal), so the servo turns
#            the face in yaw only and the pitch stays where the posture holds it.
#            The champion's forehand starts the servo (0.28 s) with the face at
#            -21 deg and sweeps it to the aim in the last 0.2 s: the pitch at
#            contact is -10 +- 12 deg and turning at 70 +- 55 deg/s, the spread
#            made by that late motion (contact pitch is uncorrelated with the
#            pitch at 0.27 s); with the ready posture at the pitch wanted the
#            arm is quiet. qa 2: the backhand only (its pitch does not follow
#            its aim at all), qa 3: the forehand only.

#   ns_k     the aim's pitch by serve speed: n_z += ns_k (|v| - ns_v0), |v| the ball's
#            predicted speed at the pad's plane. The champion's flat-arc aim puts
#            the exit elevation at the upper edge of the feasible window for fast
#            serves (a 6 m/s return must leave at 4-17 deg, the arc to the box asks
#            17) and near its centre for slow ones (4.5 m/s: 16-64 deg); a slope
#            flattens fast serves' faces (the skill's normals point at the player, so a larger n_z is a
#            more closed face: ns_k > 0 closes the face as speed rises).
#   kk       a late pelvis kick (1 on): in the last kk_t s before the ball's
#            arrival the slide's command gets an extra constant acceleration
#            along +x (away from the net) that adds kick_u m/s to the pad's
#            velocity by contact (kick_u = the target axis velocity kk_k (|v| -
#            kk_v0), clamped, less the champion's own mean pad velocity on that
#            side (kk_m1 forehand, kk_m2 backhand), over the pad normal's x),
#            costing kick_u kk_t / 2 of plane (3 cm for 0.6 m/s and 0.1 s: 1 cm of
#            ball height). It rides on the command only (set_pelvis), so the
#            parent's slide keeps its own reference and closed loop; the aim law
#            expects kk_g of the kick. Unlike pv it leaves the parent's plane
#            tracking alone (pv 2 and 3 cost the hit rate 7-20 points).

+ MyoTTV11Skill < MyoTTV10Skill
  -> read_params
    super
    @pv = param("pv", ~0.0, ~0.0, ~3.0)
    @pv_v0 = param("pv_v0", ~4.83, ~3.0, ~7.0)
    @pv_k = param("pv_k", ~0.47, ~0.0, ~2.0)
    @pv_u0 = param("pv_u0", ~0.0, ~-1.0, ~1.0)
    @pv_lo = param("pv_lo", ~0.0, ~-1.0, ~1.0)
    @pv_max = param("pv_max", ~1.2, ~0.0, ~2.5)
    @pv_g = param("pv_g", ~0.9, ~0.0, ~1.5)
    @pv_margin = param("pv_margin", ~0.0, ~-0.1, ~0.3)
    @pv_tmin = param("pv_tmin", ~0.02, ~0.01, ~0.3)
    @pv_reach = param("pv_reach", ~-0.1, ~-0.3, ~0.1)
    @pv_arm1 = param("pv_arm1", ~0.0, ~-1.0, ~1.0)
    @pv_arm2 = param("pv_arm2", ~0.0, ~-1.0, ~1.0)
    @pv_t = ~1.0
    @pv_off0 = ~-0.105
    @pv_xw_st = nil
    @kk = param("kk", ~0.0, ~0.0, ~1.0)
    @kk_t = param("kk_t", ~0.12, ~0.03, ~0.3)
    @kk_v0 = param("kk_v0", ~4.83, ~3.0, ~7.0)
    @kk_k = param("kk_k", ~0.47, ~0.0, ~2.0)
    @kk_m1 = param("kk_m1", ~0.36, ~-1.0, ~1.0)
    @kk_m2 = param("kk_m2", ~-0.23, ~-1.0, ~1.0)
    @kk_lo = param("kk_lo", ~-0.7, ~-2.0, ~0.0)
    @kk_hi = param("kk_hi", ~1.0, ~0.0, ~2.5)
    @kk_tlo = param("kk_tlo", ~-0.3, ~-1.0, ~0.5)
    @kk_thi = param("kk_thi", ~1.3, ~0.0, ~2.5)
    @kk_g = param("kk_g", ~0.9, ~0.0, ~1.5)
    @kk_amp = param("kk_amp", ~1.0, ~0.0, ~1.5)
    @ns_k = param("ns_k", ~0.0, ~-0.3, ~0.3)
    @ns_v0 = param("ns_v0", ~5.6, ~4.0, ~7.0)
    @sg = param("sg", ~0.0, ~0.0, ~1.0)
    @qa = param("qa", ~0.0, ~0.0, ~3.0)
    @qa_n = [~1.0, ~0.0, ~0.0]
    @pv_sm = param("pv_sm", ~0.4, ~0.05, ~1.0)
    @pv_h = param("pv_h", ~0.1, ~0.0, ~0.3)
    @pv_h2 = param("pv_h2", ~0.25, ~0.05, ~0.5)
    @pv_hw = param("pv_hw", ~0.1, ~0.01, ~0.4)
    @pv_arm_v = [~0.0, ~0.0, ~0.0]
    @pv_vx = ~0.0

  -> start(frame, ctl)
    super(frame, ctl)
    @pv_off0 = pad_center(frame)[0] - frame.at("env_pelvis_pos", 0)
    nil

  # ---- the pelvis as a speed governor (pv) ------------------------------------------

  # The retreat speed (m/s along +x, away from the net) planned for this serve
  # (the pad's total: the aim law expects it).
  -> pv_speed
    p = @plan
    s = Math.sqrt(p[3] * p[3] + p[4] * p[4] + p[5] * p[5])
    clamp(@pv_k * (s - @pv_v0) + @pv_u0, @pv_lo, @pv_max)

  # The pelvis's share of it (world +x speed at contact): less what the arm and
  # trunk add themselves (pv 1, 2: the constants pv_arm1 / pv_arm2; pv 3: the
  # arm's measured velocity relative to the pelvis, and the pelvis's lateral
  # velocity along the pad's normal).
  -> pv_pelvis_speed(f)
    if @pv > ~2.5
      n = pad_normal(f)
      ar = @pv_arm_v
      w = pv_arm_weight(pv_tgo(f))
      u = pv_speed - w * (ar[0] * n[0] + ar[1] * n[1] + ar[2] * n[2]) - (~0.0 - @rvy) * n[1]
      return u / clamp(n[0], ~0.5, ~1.0)
    a = @pv_arm1
    a = @pv_arm2 if @side == 2
    pv_speed - a

  # How much of the measured arm velocity counts, by the time to go: none until
  # pv_h2 s before contact, all of it pv_hw s later.
  -> pv_arm_weight(tgo)
    clamp((@pv_h2 - tgo) / @pv_hw, ~0.0, ~1.0)

  # The smoothed velocity of the arm relative to the pelvis (world).
  -> pv_track_arm(f)
    vp = paddle_velocity(f)
    i = 0
    while i < 3
      a = vp[i] - f.at("pelvis_vel", i)
      @pv_arm_v[i] = @pv_arm_v[i] + (a - @pv_arm_v[i]) * @pv_sm
      i += 1
    nil

  # pv 2: where the ball reaches the pad's plane at contact, from the base's
  # height-matching goal (xw = the pad's plane + the pelvis's distance to its
  # goal in q), and the pelvis's goal in q for it.
  -> pv_xw(f)
    @xp + pelvis_qx(f) - @gx

  # The time for the ball to reach the pad's plane where the pelvis's goal puts
  # it (the pad plane's world x when the pelvis is at @gx).
  -> pv_tgo(f)
    p = [f.at("env_ball_pos", 0), f.at("env_ball_pos", 1), f.at("env_ball_pos", 2)]
    v = [f.at("env_ball_vel", 0), f.at("env_ball_vel", 1), f.at("env_ball_vel", 2)]
    xg = @xp + pelvis_qx(f) - @gx
    c = MyoTTBall.intercept(p, v, xg, @bounced)
    return @plan[0] if c == nil
    c[0]

  # pv: the governor drives the slide from the first plan to the contact, on
  # both sides (the parent's dispatch drops the backhand's minimum-jerk slide
  # for the critically damped reference in the last 0.18 s, which is what leaves
  # the pelvis ringing at contact); v7's contact adjustments still run first.
  -> drive_pelvis(f)
    if @pv > ~0.5 && @plan != nil && @pel_mj > ~0.5
      apex_contact(f) if @ap_on > ~0.5 && !@locked && @g_hx > ~0.0
      late_contact(f) if @bh_tmin > ~0.0 && @side == 2 && !@locked && @g_hx > ~0.0
      return pv_drive(f, fly_factor > ~0.0)
    super(f)

  # drive_pelvis_fly / drive_pelvis_mj with the fore-aft slide's minimum-jerk
  # path ending at the goal AT contact with the retreat velocity (q = 1.6 - x,
  # so the reference's q-velocity is -u): jerk = 60 d / T^3 - (36 v + 24 vf)
  # / T^2 - 9 a / T; inside pv_tmin of contact it coasts.
  -> pv_drive(f, fly)
    gq = @gx
    tx = pv_tgo(f) - @pv_margin
    pv_track_arm(f) if @pv > ~2.5
    if @pv > ~1.5
      xw = pv_xw(f)
      if @locked && @pv_xw_st != nil
        xw = @pv_xw_st
      else
        @pv_xw_st = xw
      gq = ~1.6 - xw + @pv_off0 + @pv_reach
      if @pv > ~2.5
        # predictive: the pad's offset from the pelvis now plus the arm's reach over the time to go
        ar = @pv_arm_v
        h = tx
        h = @pv_h if h > @pv_h
        h = ~0.0 if h < ~0.0
        off = pad_center(f)[0] - f.at("env_pelvis_pos", 0)
        w = pv_arm_weight(tx)
        gq = ~1.6 - (xw - off - w * ar[0] * h)
      p = [f.at("env_ball_pos", 0), f.at("env_ball_pos", 1), f.at("env_ball_pos", 2)]
      v = [f.at("env_ball_vel", 0), f.at("env_ball_vel", 1), f.at("env_ball_vel", 2)]
      c = MyoTTBall.intercept(p, v, xw, @bounced)
      tx = c[0] - @pv_margin if c != nil
    @pv_t = tx
    if tx > @pv_tmin
      @pv_vx = pv_pelvis_speed(f)
      vf = ~0.0 - @pv_vx
      jx = ~60.0 * (gq - @rx) / (tx * tx * tx) - (~36.0 * @rvx + ~24.0 * vf) / (tx * tx) - ~9.0 * @rax / tx
      @rax = clamp(@rax + jx * @dt, ~0.0 - @pel_amax, @pel_amax)
    else
      @rax = ~0.0
    if fly
      ty = @plan[0] - @fly_margin
      if ty > @fly_tmin
        d = @gy - @ry
        vf2 = fly_factor * d / ty
        jy = ~60.0 * d / (ty * ty * ty) - (~36.0 * @rvy + ~24.0 * vf2) / (ty * ty) - ~9.0 * @ray / ty
        @ray = clamp(@ray + jy * @dt, ~0.0 - @pel_amax, @pel_amax)
      else
        @ray = ~0.0
    else
      tg = @plan[0] - @slide_margin
      if tg > ~0.1
        jy = ~60.0 * (@gy - @ry) / (tg * tg * tg) - ~36.0 * @rvy / (tg * tg) - ~9.0 * @ray / tg
        @ray = clamp(@ray + jy * @dt, ~0.0 - @pel_amax, @pel_amax)
      else
        w = @pel_w
        @ray = clamp(w * w * (@gy - @ry) - ~2.0 * w * @rvy, ~0.0 - @pel_amax, @pel_amax)
    @rvx = @rvx + @rax * @dt
    @rvy = @rvy + @ray * @dt
    if fly && @rvy.abs > @pel_vcap
      @rvy = clamp(@rvy, ~0.0 - @pel_vcap, @pel_vcap)
      @ray = ~0.0
    @rx = @rx + @rvx * @dt
    @ry = @ry + @rvy * @dt
    @ref_ax = ~0.0 - @rax
    @ref_ay = ~0.0 - @ray
    ex = @rx - pelvis_qx(f)
    ey = @ry - pelvis_qy(f)
    set_pelvis(@rx + @pel_fb * ex, @ry + @pel_fb * ey, @rvx, @rvy, @rax, @ray)

  # kk: the kick's speed (m/s along +x) for this serve.
  -> kick_u
    p = @plan
    s = Math.sqrt(p[3] * p[3] + p[4] * p[4] + p[5] * p[5])
    tgt = clamp(@kk_k * (s - @kk_v0), @kk_tlo, @kk_thi)
    m = @kk_m1
    m = @kk_m2 if @side == 2
    @kk_amp * clamp((tgt - m) / ~0.9, @kk_lo, @kk_hi)

  -> set_pelvis(qx, qy, vx, vy, ax, ay)
    if @kk > ~0.5 && @plan != nil && @side != 0
      te = @kk_t - @plan[0]
      if te > ~0.0
        u = kick_u
        a = u / @kk_t
        v = a * te
        d = ~0.5 * a * te * te
        return super(qx - d * (~1.0 + @pel_fb), qy, vx - v, vy, ax - a, ay)
    super(qx, qy, vx, vy, ax, ay)

  # qa: the aim law's normal at the pad's own pitch.
  -> before(f, ctl)
    @qa_n = pad_normal(f)
    super(f, ctl)

  -> aim_normal(plan)
    n = super(plan)
    if @ns_k != ~0.0 && @side != 0
      sp = Math.sqrt(plan[3] * plan[3] + plan[4] * plan[4] + plan[5] * plan[5])
      nz = n[2] + @ns_k * (sp - @ns_v0)
      h0 = Math.sqrt(n[0] * n[0] + n[1] * n[1])
      if h0 > ~0.01
        k = Math.sqrt(clamp(~1.0 - nz * nz, ~0.0, ~1.0)) / h0
        n = [n[0] * k, n[1] * k, nz]
    return n if @qa < ~0.5 || @side == 0
    return n if @qa > ~2.5 && @side != 1
    return n if @qa > ~1.5 && @qa < ~2.5 && @side != 2
    nz = @qa_n[2]
    h = Math.sqrt(n[0] * n[0] + n[1] * n[1])
    return n if h < ~0.01
    k = Math.sqrt(clamp(~1.0 - nz * nz, ~0.0, ~1.0)) / h
    [n[0] * k, n[1] * k, nz]

  # sg: the servo works on the ball's state at the goal plane.
  -> servo(f, pc, plan, ey)
    if @sg > ~0.5 && plan != nil && @g_hx > ~0.5
      p = [f.at("env_ball_pos", 0), f.at("env_ball_pos", 1), f.at("env_ball_pos", 2)]
      v = [f.at("env_ball_vel", 0), f.at("env_ball_vel", 1), f.at("env_ball_vel", 2)]
      c = MyoTTBall.intercept(p, v, pv_xw(f), @bounced)
      return super(f, pc, c, ey) if c != nil
    super(f, pc, plan, ey)

  # the governor's lock-time report ("pv:" u : reference q-velocity : reference q : time to go : goal q)
  -> lock_now(ctl)
    super(ctl)
    if @pv > ~0.5 && @plan != nil
      ctl.emit("pv:" + [pv_speed, @rvx, @rx, @pv_t, @gx, @pv_vx, @pv_arm_v[0], @pv_arm_v[1], @pv_arm_v[2]].map(->(x) x.to_s).join(":"))
    nil

  # The aim law expects the retreat: the planned speed until the last 0.12 s,
  # then the slide reference's own velocity.
  -> pad_vel_expected
    v = super
    if @kk > ~0.5 && @plan != nil && @side != 0 && !((fam_side_on && @fam > 0) || @fam >= 5)
      v = [v[0] + @kk_g * kick_u, v[1], v[2]]
    return v if @pv < ~0.5 || @plan == nil || (fam_side_on && @fam > 0) || @fam >= 5
    if @pv > ~2.5
      # the pad's predicted world velocity: the pelvis's terminal velocity plus the arm's
      w = pv_arm_weight(@pv_t)
      ar = @pv_arm_v
      return [v[0] + @pv_g * (@pv_vx + w * ar[0]), v[1] + @pv_g * ((~0.0 - @rvy) + w * ar[1]), v[2] + @pv_g * w * ar[2]]
    u = pv_speed
    u = ~0.0 - @rvx if @pv_t < ~0.12
    [v[0] + @pv_g * u, v[1], v[2]]
